// Title: Browser Started with Remote Debugging
// Sigma ID: b3d34dc5-2efd-4ae3-845f-8ec14921f449
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: pH-T (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-27 | Modified: 2022-12-23
// ATT&CK: credential-access, collection, T1185
// Description: Detects browsers starting with the remote debugging flags. Which is a technique often used to
//   perform browser injection attacks
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20230420012250/https://yoroi.company/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/EternityGroup_report_compressed.pdf
//   - https://www.mdsec.co.uk/2022/10/analysing-lastpass-part-1/
//   - https://github.com/defaultnamehere/cookie_crimes/
//   - https://github.com/wunderwuzzi23/firefox-cookiemonster
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/03f5200b4cc909d074354889a71e917ab40ec911/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_browsers_remote_debugging.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains " --remote-debugging-" or (FolderPath endswith "\\firefox.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -start-debugger-server")
